{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (Task #5147) to implement srd016-dirname R3.1-R3.3 (error handling and exit codes) for `cmd/dirname`. Specifically:\n   - R3.1: Exit code 0 on successful execution\n   - R3.2: Error message to stderr when no operand is provided, exit 1\n   - R3.3: Exit code non-zero (1) when a write error occurs on stdout\n   \n   The task specifies modifying `cmd/dirname/main.go` (add error handling) and `cmd/dirname/dirname_test.go` (add differential test cases for error conditions). The task includes detailed execution constitution, go style constitution, package contracts, and acceptance criteria (AC1-AC4).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gdirname`) via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Binary name normalization in tests using regex to match both `dirname` and `gdirname` in error messages\n   - The cobbler-scaffold pipeline: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation)\n   - Git is managed externally by orchestrator — NO git commands allowed\n   - Write-all-then-build strategy (no incremental compile-fix loops)\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for usage errors and write failures\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd016-dirname.yaml`\n     - The SRD defining all dirname requirements (R1-R4)\n     - R3 section defines error handling: R3.1 (exit 0 success), R3.2 (exit 1 + stderr on no args), R3.3 (exit 1 on write error)\n   \n   - `cmd/dirname/main.go` (existing, 89 lines)\n     - Already implements R3.1-R3.3:\n     - R3.2 handling (lines 39-43):\n  